.TH INTRO 2
.SH NAME
intro \- introduction to system calls and libraries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B import "vsys:libuser"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vectra's programs are written in Odin.
A program under
.B cmd/
or
.B sys/libuser/programs
begins at
.BR _start ,
which the loader calls with a pointer to the arguments the kernel wrote
onto its stack:
.IP
.EX
@(export, link_name = "_start")
start :: proc "c" (block: ^abi.Args) {
	context = libuser.startup()
	main(libuser.args(block))
}
.EE
.PP
.I Libuser.startup
runs the Odin runtime with an empty context, then answers a
.B runtime.Context
whose allocator is the program's heap (see below), and whose temporary
allocator is that same heap, because a program has no separate arena.
.I Libuser.args
turns the kernel's record into an Odin
.B []string ,
the program's own name first, by the caller's convention: the kernel adds
nothing to it.
.PP
Every package a program imports names a
.I collection
called
.BR vsys: ,
so
.B import "vsys:libuser"
finds
.B sys/libuser
wherever the tree is checked out, and the same prefix names every other
library below.
.SS Descriptors
A program starts with descriptors 0, 1 and 2 open on whatever its parent
arranged, its arguments on its stack, and the namespace and environment its
parent chose.
.I Rfork
makes a second process, sharing or copying each of those by a flag, and
.I exec
replaces the running program in place;
.I spawn
does both in one call.
See
.IR fork (2)
and
.IR exec (2).
.SS Answers and errors
A system call is one wrapper in
.B sys/libuser/sys.odin
around a single instruction.
Its answer is the kernel's own signed number: zero or more is a result, a
count or a descriptor, and a negative number is
.B \-errno
out of
.BR sys/vectra9 's
.B Errno
table.
There is no per-process error buffer to swap, as Plan 9's
.I errstr
keeps;
a caller that wants an error's name passes the failed call's own answer to
.IR errstr (2).
.PP
A process ends by calling
.I exits
with a string, empty for success and a few words otherwise.
Its parent collects the string with
.IR await .
See
.IR wait (2).
.SS The libraries under sys/
.TP
